# Pickle Rick

Date: 17 August 2026

Platform: TryHackMe

Room: Pickle Rick

Skills Learnt:

1. Used Nmap to scan the target and understand what ports and services were running.
2. Used dirsearch for directory enumeration and to find hidden pages and files on the website.
3. Used curl to quickly check web pages and files directly from the terminal.
4. Did a lot of web forensics by checking the page source, HTML comments, robots.txt and other exposed files for useful information.
5. Practiced finding hidden credentials and using small clues from different places to progress through the room.
6. Got more comfortable with Linux navigation, file searching and checking permissions after getting access to the system.
7. Learnt how web enumeration, web forensics and Linux enumeration can all be used together in one challenge.

Notes:

This room was mostly focused on web enumeration and web forensics. I started by scanning the machine with Nmap, then used dirsearch and curl to look around the web server and check files that were not obvious from the main page.

A big part of the challenge was just investigating properly. I checked the source code, HTML comments, robots.txt and different files for clues, then used the information I found to get further access.

After that, I had to look around the Linux system, search through files and directories and figure out where the remaining ingredients were stored.

I liked this room because it felt more practical than the basic rooms. Instead of being given everything directly, I had to find small pieces of information and connect them together.
